<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Golden Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1830</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Harmandir Sahib</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Golden Temple, or Harmandir Sahib, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a> is the holiest shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikhism</a>. Under the patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> it was covered in gold leaf, a project completed around 1830, and it remains the defining monument of Sikh civilisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-temple.jpg" alt="Golden Temple" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shagil Kannur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Golden_Temple_of_Amrithsar_7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
